IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cr1-interpretation`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), PART III -- EMPLOYMENT INCLUDED IN OR EXCEPTED FROM
-- PENSIONABLE EMPLOYMENT BY REGULATION: regulation 15, the interpretation of Part III. Piece cr1. LAYER 1.
--
-- The four definitions of 15(1) ("employer operating in Canada", "employment in international transportation",
-- "establishment in Canada", "ship") are used by regulations 16 to 34.1. "employer operating in Canada includes
-- (a) to (d)": the list is open, so a case outside it answers NOTHING (the same reading as the keel's fork F4 and
-- this piece's F1). The other three definitions "mean" and are closed.
-- Paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act (employment by a province brought in by agreement) belongs to piece cp1; whether
-- a province's employment "has been included in pensionable employment by regulation in accordance with"
-- it is a plain input here (-- out of range: section 7 (piece cp1)).

§ `Regulations, Part III -- regulation 15: interpretation`

§§ `Regulation 15(1): employer operating in Canada`

-- src:222 | employer operating in Canada includes
-- src:223 | (a) Her Majesty in right of Canada,
-- src:224 | (b) Her Majesty in right of a province, if employment by Her Majesty in right of that province has been included in pensionable employment by regulation in accordance with paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act,
-- src:225 | (c) an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province, if employment by that agent has been included in pensionable employment by regulation in accordance with paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act, and
-- src:226 | (d) any employer who has an establishment in Canada and who
-- src:227 | (i) is subject to income tax under Part I of the Income Tax Act, or
-- src:228 | (ii) but for section 149 of the Income Tax Act, would be subject to income tax under Part I of that Act,
-- src:229 | for any taxation year for which he has taxable income; (employeur exerçant des opérations au Canada)
@ref Reg 15(1) "employer operating in Canada" (src:222-229)
DECLARE `cr1 Kind of employer for the definition of employer operating in Canada` IS ONE OF
    `Her Majesty in right of Canada`
    `Her Majesty in right of a province`
    `an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province`
    `another kind of employer`

-- (a) Her Majesty in right of Canada; (b) Her Majesty in right of a province, or (c) an agent of Her Majesty in
-- right of a province, if employment by Her Majesty or the agent has been included in pensionable employment by
-- regulation in accordance with paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act; (d) any employer who has an establishment in
-- Canada and who is subject to income tax under Part I of the Income Tax Act, or but for section 149 of that Act
-- would be, for any taxation year for which the employer has taxable income.
@ref Reg 15(1) "employer operating in Canada" (src:222-229)
GIVEN kind IS A `cr1 Kind of employer for the definition of employer operating in Canada`
      `employment by that employer has been included in pensionable employment by regulation in accordance with paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has an establishment in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is subject to income tax under Part I of the Income Tax Act, or but for section 149 of that Act would be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has taxable income for the taxation year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(1) — an employer is an employer operating in Canada` kind `employment by that employer has been included in pensionable employment by regulation in accordance with paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act` `the employer has an establishment in Canada` `the employer is subject to income tax under Part I of the Income Tax Act, or but for section 149 of that Act would be` `the employer has taxable income for the taxation year` MEANS
    IF (    (kind EQUALS `Her Majesty in right of Canada`)
         OR (    (kind EQUALS `Her Majesty in right of a province` OR kind EQUALS `an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province`)
             AND `employment by that employer has been included in pensionable employment by regulation in accordance with paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act`)
         OR (    `the employer has an establishment in Canada`
             AND `the employer is subject to income tax under Part I of the Income Tax Act, or but for section 149 of that Act would be`
             AND `the employer has taxable income for the taxation year`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 15(1): employment in international transportation`

-- src:230 | employment in international transportation means employment that is primarily engaged in by a person in a pay period and that is performed partly within and partly outside Canada on
-- src:231 | (a) a ship,
-- src:232 | (b) an aircraft used in the operation of a commercial air service by a person who is licensed to operate an international service under the Canada Transportation Act,
-- src:233 | (c) a freight or passenger train, or
-- src:234 | (d) a motor vehicle that is registered to operate in one or more provinces of Canada and in one or more states of the United States; (emploi dans le transport international)
@ref Reg 15(1) "employment in international transportation" (src:230-234)
DECLARE `cr1 Conveyance in the definition of employment in international transportation` IS ONE OF
    `a ship`
    `an aircraft used in the operation of a commercial air service by a person who is licensed to operate an international service under the Canada Transportation Act`
    `a freight or passenger train`
    `a motor vehicle that is registered to operate in one or more provinces of Canada and in one or more states of the United States`
    `another conveyance`

-- employment in international transportation means employment that is primarily engaged in by a person in a pay
-- period and that is performed partly within and partly outside Canada on (a) a ship, (b) such an aircraft, (c) a
-- freight or passenger train, or (d) such a motor vehicle.
@ref Reg 15(1) "employment in international transportation" (src:230-234)
GIVEN conveyance IS A `cr1 Conveyance in the definition of employment in international transportation`
      `the employment is primarily engaged in by the person in a pay period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is performed partly within and partly outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 15(1) — employment is employment in international transportation` conveyance `the employment is primarily engaged in by the person in a pay period` `the employment is performed partly within and partly outside Canada` MEANS
    CONSIDER conveyance
    WHEN `another conveyance` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `the employment is primarily engaged in by the person in a pay period` AND `the employment is performed partly within and partly outside Canada`

§§ `Regulation 15(1): establishment in Canada and ship`

-- establishment in Canada, with respect to an employer, means any office, warehouse, factory, oil well, gas
-- well, mine, workshop, farm, timber land, pier, wharf, school, college, club, residence, hotel, motel,
-- restaurant, tavern, bar or any other place or premises in Canada that is owned, leased or licensed by the
-- employer and where the employer or one or more of the employees works or reports for work or from or at
-- which one or more of the employees are paid. The list ends "or any other place or premises", so the listed
-- kinds add nothing to the test: any place or premises that meets the three conditions is one.
-- src:235 | establishment in Canada, with respect to an employer, means any office, warehouse, factory, oil well, gas well, mine, workshop, farm, timber land, pier, wharf, school, college, club, residence, hotel, motel, restaurant, tavern, bar or any other place or premises in Canada that is owned, leased or licensed by the employer and where the employer or one or more of his employees works or reports for work or from or at which one or more of his employees are paid; (établissement au Canada)
@ref Reg 15(1) "establishment in Canada" (src:235)
GIVEN `the place or premises is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place or premises is owned, leased or licensed by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer or one or more of the employer's employees works or reports for work there` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one or more of the employer's employees are paid from or at it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 15(1) — a place is an establishment in Canada of an employer` `the place or premises is in Canada` `the place or premises is owned, leased or licensed by the employer` `the employer or one or more of the employer's employees works or reports for work there` `one or more of the employer's employees are paid from or at it` MEANS
        `the place or premises is in Canada`
    AND `the place or premises is owned, leased or licensed by the employer`
    AND (    `the employer or one or more of the employer's employees works or reports for work there`
         OR  `one or more of the employer's employees are paid from or at it`)

-- src:236 | ship means a vessel, boat or craft, used or designed to be used in navigation in, on, through or immediately above water. (navire)
@ref Reg 15(1) "ship" (src:236)
GIVEN `a vessel, boat or craft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `used or designed to be used in navigation in, on, through or immediately above water` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 15(1) — a craft is a ship` `a vessel, boat or craft` `used or designed to be used in navigation in, on, through or immediately above water` MEANS
    `a vessel, boat or craft` AND `used or designed to be used in navigation in, on, through or immediately above water`

§§ `Regulation 15(2)`

-- 15 (2) All other words and expressions in this Part have the same meaning as in Part I.
-- src:237 | (2) All other words and expressions in this Part have the same meaning as in Part I.
@ref Reg 15(2) (src:237)
GIVEN part IS A `cr1 Part of the Regulations`
GIVETH A MAYBE `cr1 Part of the Regulations`
`reg 15(2) — the Part whose words and expressions Part III uses for the words it does not define` part MEANS
    CONSIDER part
    WHEN `the Regulations' Part III` THEN JUST `the Regulations' Part I`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
